        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-channel): add timeout to qa-bus state guarded fetch",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `getQaBusState` called `fetchWithSsrFGuard` with no `timeoutMs` and no `AbortSignal`, so a loopback qa-bus peer that accepted TCP but never returned headers could hang Gateway/QA tooling forever (body idle caps never start).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Pass `timeoutMs: QA_BUS_STATE_TIMEOUT_MS` (10s) through the existing guarded fetch, matching Feishu registration / similar Type C hang floors.\n- Optional `options.timeoutMs` overrides for hermetic hang regressions only; production callers omit it.\n- No new config/env surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** A hung qa-bus `/v1/state` peer could pin state inspection indefinitely.\n\n**After:** State fetches fail closed after 10s with `TimeoutError` so QA/monitor loops can continue.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCompete: no open PR for `getQaBusState` / `qa-channel.bus-state` / `path:extensions/qa-channel/src/bus-client.ts`.\n\nHead: `24ccd1e2f0d7e485c4faa3e37c0a1be149438e9f`\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-channel/src/bus-client.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n[qa-channel bus-state hang proof] timed_out=true name=TimeoutError elapsed_ms=87 production_timeout_ms=10000\nTests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\nNegative control: same never-headers fixture without `timeoutMs` would hang past the test's outer bound; with the 80ms override, timeout arrives in ~87ms.",
